  <!--
    Not compiled on Linux:
    - MonoDevelop.Refactoring/CommandArgsFactories.cs, MonoDevelop.Refactoring/StreamingFindUsagesPresenter.cs:
      Roslyn EditorFeatures types (GoToImplementationCommandArgs, IStreamingFindUsagesPresenter) used only by the
      Cocoa/WPF MonoDevelop.TextEditor command handlers (excluded, ADR 0012; EditorFeatures is not referenced, T089).
      The GTK editor runs Find References / Go to Implementation through RefactoringService and FindReferencesProvider.
    - MonoDevelop.Refactoring.Options/* (except Util.cs): the code style option view models are built on the Roslyn 3
      options API (OptionSet, CodeStyleOption<T>, IOptionService, PreviewWorkspace) that Roslyn 4+ replaced with
      editorconfig-based options; code style is configured with .editorconfig (Ide EditorConfigService).
  -->

